  data: {
    LLM: "Identify the 10-multiples immediately. Face cards are your best friends because they count as 10, making it very easy to hit the 20 or 30 mark for your foundation. If you have two 10s and a 5, you need another 5 to make a foundation; if you don't have it, you likely have 'No Niu'.\n\nThe 'High Card' Tie-Breaker: If both you and the banker have the same Niu value (e.g., Niu 7), the winner is decided by the highest individual card. Therefore, having a King increases your win probability significantly even if your hand point-value is mediocre.\n\nBankroll Management: Because Niu Niu often features 'Double' or 'Triple' payouts for Niu 7 or higher, a single bad round as the banker can wipe out your entire stack. Strategic players often choose to 'Bank' only when they have enough capital to survive a Niu Niu sweep.",
    Player: "Identify the 10-multiples immediately. Face cards are your best friends because they count as 10, making it very easy to hit the 20 or 30 mark for your foundation. If you have two 10s and a 5, you need another 5 to make a foundation; if you don't have it, you likely have 'No Niu'.\n\nThe 'High Card' Tie-Breaker: If both you and the banker have the same Niu value (e.g., Niu 7), the winner is decided by the highest individual card. Therefore, having a King increases your win probability significantly even if your hand point-value is mediocre.\n\nBankroll Management: Because Niu Niu often features 'Double' or 'Triple' payouts for Niu 7 or higher, a single bad round as the banker can wipe out your entire stack. Strategic players often choose to 'Bank' only when they have enough capital to survive a Niu Niu sweep.",
